rise the fused KERNEL at every N (so production thresholds can be\ncalibrated), the per-codec production N-thresholds are forced wide open.\n\nUsage:\n  PYTHONPATH=$(pwd) ./.venv/bin/python benchmark_codec_decision.py\n  ... --synthetic --check --n-values 1,64,256\n  ... --csv codec_decision.csv\n  ... --codecs zipserv,p4flat --projs o,gate_up\n  ... --ats --codecs p4flat --projs gate_up   # GH200: exp->LPDDR/C2C, mant->HBM\n\nWith ``--ats`` (GH200 only) the codec's compressed-exponent stream is relocated\nto Grace LPDDR (the raw sign|mantissa byte stream stays in HBM) and BOTH\ncompressed strategies are re-measured reading that exponent over the NVLink-C2C\nlink, adding two iso/h2d column groups:\n\n  * decmpATS  — decompress (exponent from LPDDR/C2C, mantissa from HBM) into a\n                dense bf16 weight in HBM, then cuBLAS GEMM (still an HBM write).\n  * fusedATS  — fused decode+GEMM; the exponent streams from LPDDR straight into\n                the SMs, no dense-weight HBM staging at all.\n\nThis gives the direct HBM-vs-C2C comparison for the decomp+GEMM and fused paths\nalike.  See\n``ats-benchmarks/benchmarks/compress/python/bf16_split_decompress_ats.py``.\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --codecs CODECS\n  --projs PROJS\n  --n-values N_VALUES\n  --tp TP               tensor-parallel degree (shards shapes; needs\n                        --synthetic for tp>1)\n  --synthetic           random bf16 weights instead of the real checkpoint\n  --weights-dir WEIGHTS_DIR\n  --shards SHARDS       max safetensor shards to scan for real weights\n  --layers LAYERS       comma-separated real checkpoint layers; official\n                        scaling run uses the outlier-heavy 0 and\n                        representative 40\n  --layer LAYER         legacy single-layer override for --layers\n  --repeat-id REPEAT_ID\n                        independent-process repeat recorded in every CSV row\n  --seed SEED           base seed for reproducible BF16 activations\n  --warmup WARMUP\n  --iters ITERS\n  --no-flush            disable L2 flush between iters\n  --no-h2d              skip the concurrent-H2D contention condition\n  --h2d-bytes H2D_BYTES\n                        H2D contention traffic per copy (0 = codec compressed\n                        size)\n  --check               print per-row fused OK/INVALID marker (validity gate\n                        is always on unless --no-validate)\n  --no-validate         skip the fused bit-exactness gate (trust fused\n                        timings)\n  --full-model          print per-layer / full-model strategy totals\n  --ats                 also measure the fused GEMM with the compressed\n                        exponent in Grace LPDDR (mantissa in HBM), read by the\n                        SMs over NVLink-C2C/ATS (no HBM staging). GH200 only.\n                        Adds 'fusedATS' columns.\n  --ats-pool-gib ATS_POOL_GIB\n                        LPDDR ATS pool size per projection (GiB)\n  --ats-hugepage-dir ATS_HUGEPAGE_DIR\n                        hugetlbfs mount for the ATS pool; falls back to\n                        numa_alloc_onnode if no free hugepages\n  --ats-lpddr-node ATS_LPDDR_NODE\n                        NUMA node for the LPDDR fallback (Grace = 0 on GH200)\n  --csv CSV             output CSV; required so official cells cannot be lost\n"},"started_at_ms":1788516421263,"completed_at_ms":1788516423286}}
